      <header class="index__section-header">
        <span class="index__section-label">WHY BANGLADESH</span>
        <h2 class="index__section-title">Why Global Fashion Brands Choose Bangladesh Clothing Manufacturers</h2>
        <p class="index__section-subtitle">Bangladesh is the world's second-largest apparel exporter — and there are structural reasons why the world's most demanding brands source here.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="index__grid index__grid--3" style="margin-bottom:1px;">
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Cost Structure</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Production costs in Bangladesh run 30 to 40 percent below equivalent quality production in China and 20 to 30 percent below Vietnam — driven by lower labour costs, vertically integrated supply chains, and competitive raw material access. For brands producing 5,000 to 50,000 pieces per season, the saving is material.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Duty Access</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Bangladesh garments enter the EU and UK under Generalised Scheme of Preferences (GSP) arrangements, meaning zero or near-zero import duty for qualifying buyers. For a brand importing $200,000 of apparel into the EU, the duty saving can exceed $20,000 per season compared with China-origin goods.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Certification Density</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Bangladesh has the highest concentration of LEED-certified green garment factories globally and a strong cluster of GOTS, OEKO-TEX, BSCI, and SA8000 certified manufacturers. For brands with sustainability commitments or EU Digital Product Passport obligations, Bangladesh-origin certified production is both available and cost-competitive.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index__grid index__grid--3">
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Skilled Workforce</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Bangladesh has over four million trained garment workers concentrated in Dhaka, Narayanganj, Gazipur, and Chittagong — the highest density of apparel production expertise in South Asia. This workforce specialisation translates directly into consistent stitch quality, lower defect rates, and faster operator training curves on new styles.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Speed to Port</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Chittagong is Bangladesh's primary export port, handling over 90 percent of the country's garment exports. Transit to major EU ports runs 22 to 28 days by sea. Air freight from Dhaka to London, Amsterdam, or New York takes 2 to 5 days. For brands managing tight seasonal windows, the logistics infrastructure is well-tested and reliable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Compliance Infrastructure</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Following factory safety reforms after 2013, Bangladesh's RMG sector invested heavily in building compliance infrastructure — fire safety, structural engineering, worker welfare, and audit readiness. SDF Clothing holds 13 international certifications covering quality, environment, social compliance, and organic textile standards, audited and renewed annually.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
